      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Given that $F=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j,$ what is $\\text{div}\\,F?$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=\u2207\\cdot F=\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\cdot F & =\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "20a416be-740c-58f7-b2fc-8e97f4f8f7c0",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{x+y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "23093b8a-a47d-569c-a492-694f3c166fff",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "(x+y)\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "6a0c18e8-462f-530b-8c14-87f6c37a812f",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "(x-y)\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "20188645-3170-5765-97f2-269ad7df2add",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{2x-2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}"
